WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.110
- So, Neil, what is the
coolest new science thing

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.790
you've learned to tell me?

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.690
- I've learned cool
science things every day.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.630
And sometimes I have to be
(laughing) reminded of them.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.270
Maybe I knew them long ago.
- Yeah.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.000
- Like we all knew that we have very,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.470
a high common DNA with
chimpanzees, like 99% identical.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.303
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And you say, okay,

00:00:19.303 --> 00:00:20.220
I get that,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.220
but do you know we also have
50% common DNA with a banana?

00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:26.953
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.953 --> 00:00:28.332
- I do love bananas.
- Okay?

00:00:28.332 --> 00:00:30.510
- My son, all he eats is bananas.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.343
- [Neil] There you go.

00:00:31.343 --> 00:00:32.620
And I got one other for ya, you ready?

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.560
If you look at the Tree of Life,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.740
the common ancestors
between humans and mushrooms

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.040
split after--

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.193
- What kind of mushrooms?

00:00:43.193 --> 00:00:45.250
(all laughing)

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.120
- After the common ancestor

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
between our common
ancestor and green plants,

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:55.520
which means we and mushrooms
are more genetically connected

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.850
than either of us are to green plants.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.040
- What?
- I know.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.820
- We are like fungus sometimes.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.837
- [Neil] We are a fungus among us, yeah.

00:01:02.837 --> 00:01:03.891
- We are like fungus sometimes.

00:01:03.891 --> 00:01:05.009
- And--

00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:05.842
- [Lucy] Interesting.

00:01:05.842 --> 00:01:07.611
- And some people have whole
relationships with mushrooms.

00:01:07.611 --> 00:01:08.444
(audience laughs)

00:01:08.444 --> 00:01:09.635
- You know?
- Yes.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:10.468
- You know what?
- That's what I'm sayin'.

00:01:10.468 --> 00:01:11.607
- I know those people.
- [Lucy] Yes.

00:01:11.607 --> 00:01:12.440
(Neil laughs)

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.040
- And I'm like, be around people you love

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:14.873
and that love you.

00:01:14.873 --> 00:01:15.706
- So, these are new facts.

00:01:15.706 --> 00:01:17.630
I'm more likely to learn
a new fact in a science

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.089
that's not my specialty.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:19.089 --> 00:01:21.150
- So, but I love learning.
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.990
If it's out of my specialty with science,

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:24.385
I'm just totally lost.

00:01:24.385 --> 00:01:26.191
(all laughing)

